{"type": "provenance", "schema": "gw2-frida-ode-edge-sample/1", "what": "runtime probe of a **DiffEq (Mode::Ode)** match **with the five stop exits judged at run time**: per shot, the sampler arguments (mode/flip/x0/y0/step + the token stream actually fed in), the returned point array (ptr, n, digest, first/last point), **which of the five stop exits fired** (breakpoint on the deciding instruction of each), and the point the report reads (`pos = pts[n-1]` at execute_results 0x472865).", "stop_judgement": {"why": "dispatch/40 could only infer the stop reason from OUR OWN trace; 2 of the 5 exits (budget exhausted / 100 bisections without convergence) were never observed. This probe judges them from two **non-branch** breakpoints plus the sampler frame, so `stop.kind` is a runtime fact.", "judged_at": {"OverX_OverY_NaN": "gw+0x3c2840 = accept-path entry (entered only when 0.001 > |chord-step|, once per accepted point). Inside, the binary checks in order `ucomisd px,cand_y`+jp (NaN) -> `|mid|>25` -> `|cand_y|>15`; the handler re-evaluates the same three predicates from the frame slots the binary loads into xmm0/xmm1 (mid@rsp+0x80, cand_y@rsp+0x50).", "Budget_NoConverge": "gw+0x3c2b5d = shared epilogue (every exit and the normal end jump here, exactly once per call). count == budget (r12d == r13d, both read at the epilogue) => Budget; count < budget and no accept-path exit was recorded => NoConverge (the bisection used up all 100 iterations)."}, "not_hooked": [{"rva": "0x3c2835", "instr": "jmp 0x3c2b5d (hi=mid branch exhausted ebx=100)", "why": "hooking an unconditional jmp makes it fire on EVERY call (even n=1), see docs/06 29.7"}, {"rva": "0x3c2679", "instr": "je 0x3c2b5d (lo=mid branch exhausted)", "why": "same class of instruction; also too hot (per iteration)"}, {"rva": "0x3c291e", "instr": "jmp 0x3c2b5d (count == budget)", "why": "same class of instruction; the epilogue rule covers it"}], "exits": [{"kind": "OverX", "rva": "0x3c28a0", "instr": "ja 0x3c2b5d (ucomisd 25.0,|mid|)", "hooked": "re-evaluated at 0x3c2840"}, {"kind": "OverY", "rva": "0x3c28bc", "instr": "ja 0x3c2b5d (ucomisd 15.0,|cand_y|)", "hooked": "re-evaluated at 0x3c2840"}, {"kind": "NaN", "rva": "0x3c2881", "instr": "jp 0x3c2b5d (ucomisd xmm1,xmm0)", "hooked": "re-evaluated at 0x3c2840", "note": "UNREACHABLE in Mode::Ode: entering the accept path already requires a finite |chord-step|, and hypot(h, cand_y-y) is NaN whenever cand_y is NaN (docs/06 29.6). 0 hits in every run."}, {"kind": "NoConverge", "rva": "0x3c2835 / 0x3c2679", "instr": "jmp/je 0x3c2b5d", "hooked": "judged at 0x3c2b5d (count < budget, no accept-path exit)"}, {"kind": "Budget", "rva": "0x3c291e", "instr": "jmp 0x3c2b5d after cmp r12d,r13d", "hooked": "judged at 0x3c2b5d (count == budget)"}], "cross_checks": ["stop.count + 1 == n (points accepted, first point excluded)", "Budget: stop.count == stop.budget (read from r12d/r13d at the epilogue)", "probe self-test (stopSelfTest at install) feeds 14 synthetic frame/register sets through the SAME classifier: each exit is recognised and the near misses (exactly 25.0 / exactly 15.0 / NaN vs `ja` / count != budget) are rejected", "arrays are re-integrated by examples/ode_array_check: bitwise identical, same length"]}, "how_to_make_an_ode_match": {"path": "campaign: user://campaign.save = \"level_20\" (unlock all 21) -> Menu \"Campaign\" -> level node #16 (691,751) -> popup \"Start\" (1072,1009). Campaign level 16 has func=1 (DiffEq) per docs/10-campaign.md 4 (mode word 0x05030001, bit-exact).", "ui_check": "the JoinLevelPopUp shows the `dy/dx =` icon and the play screen prompt reads `dy/dx =` instead of `f(x) =` (screenshots, not committed)"}, "build": {"game": "Graphwar II Linux 2.0.60 (Steam)", "libgraphwarrust.so_sha256": "9a53811518e74b7575c1b9dd1f21cdd1f4f015bfdcd8eaeee4dfdf0bcabed187", "engine": "Godot 4.7.stable.official + godot-rust (API v4.6, runtime v4.7)", "address_space": "RVA = ELF virtual address = module offset; Ghidra address = RVA + 0x100000", "hooked_rva": {"sampler_calculate": "0x3c2530", "evaluate": "0x4eb9d0", "execute_results": "0x472470", "exec_queue_probe": "0x4724cc", "pos_read_movdqu": "0x472865", "slot_9bac98": "0x9bac98", "ode_exits": {"no_converge_hi": "0x3c2835", "no_converge_lo": "0x3c2679", "nan": "0x3c2881", "over_x": "0x3c28a0", "over_y": "0x3c28bc", "budget": "0x3c291e", "epilogue": "0x3c2b5d"}}}, "how": {"harness": "Xvfb :92 -screen 0 1920x1160x24 -listen tcp -ac (+ mesa-only EGL/GLX env)", "driver": "tools/frida_ode_edge.py --attach (NOT frida spawn: spawn hangs the game in wait4)", "probe": "tools/frida_ode_edge.js (read-only Interceptor hooks; no memory writes)", "sampler_abi": "0x3c2530 (out: Vec<(f64,f64)> = rdi, tokens: &TokenBuf{cap,ptr,len} = rsi, flip = edx, MODE = ecx [0=Normal, 1=Ode], x0 = xmm0, y0 = xmm1, step = xmm2). Read off the prologue (3c2541/3c2544/3c254a/3c254c/3c254f/3c2555/3c255a) and the 0x3c25f5 `test %r15b,%r15b` split into two bisection loops.", "digest": "FNV-1a 64 over ALL 16*n bytes (`digest_xy`) and over the y halves only (`digest_y`).", "positive_control": "probe self-test at install: two 100-point synthetic arrays -> same; flip 1 bit at point 37 -> diffPoints=1; flip one more at point 90 -> 2. Also runtime: different (text, constant) gives different arrays.", "mode_evidence": "(1) `ecx` at the sampler entry reads 1 for every shot; (2) the evaluator receives many DISTINCT y arguments (Normal passes y0 once, then 0); (3) the UI shows `dy/dx =`."}, "cut": "per shot: the expression typed (host marker), mode/flip/x0/y0/step, the token stream fed to the sampler ({tag, value-bits}), the array the report reads (ptr, n, digest, first/last/second-last point) **with the stop exit that fired**, the other sampler calls of the same shot, the execute_results queue snapshot, and the 16 bytes read by the `movdqu` (pos_x/pos_y).", "dropped": "beat rows, whole-array hex, and every evaluator sample except the first few.", "no_local_paths": "no filesystem path and no user name; pointers are ASLR-random per run.", "sources": [{"label": "l17_obstacle", "raw_jsonl_sha256": "4c802fb3967a736778951a1d4c3bf8d8ae5be2f10cd42d3dbe7c69f22aa3db42", "raw_jsonl_lines": 74, "records_by_type": {"cfg_ack": 1, "selftest": 1, "hooks": 1, "beat": 53, "marker": 3, "calc": 6, "exec_enter": 3, "exec_queue": 3, "pos_read": 3}, "shots": 3}], "probe_selftest_at_install": {"array_compare": {"identical_reports_same": true, "onebit_reports_diff": true, "twobit_reports_diff": true, "detail": {"same": true, "one": 1, "two": 2}}, "stop_classifier": {"cases": 14, "bad": [], "ok": true}}, "hooks": {"type": "hooks", "base": "7fd475e00000", "size": 10241312, "hooks": [{"name": "sampler", "rva": "0x3c2530"}, {"name": "ode_accept_entry", "rva": "gw+3c2840", "why": "接受路径入口：按 0x3c2881/0x3c28a0/0x3c28bc 的顺序复算 NaN / |mid|>25 / |cand_y|>15"}, {"name": "ode_epilogue", "rva": "gw+3c2b5d"}, {"name": "evaluate", "rva": "0x4eb9d0"}, {"name": "execute_results", "rva": "0x472470"}, {"name": "exec_queue", "rva": "0x4724cc"}, {"name": "pos_read", "rva": "0x472865"}], "slot_sampler": {"addr": "7fd4767bac98", "raw": "30251c76d47f0000200c2676d47f0000", "target": "7fd4761c2530", "target_rva": "gw+3c2530"}}, "counts": {"shots": 3, "distinct_modes": [1], "shots_with_repro": 3, "repro_bitwise_identical": 3, "pos_read_with_n": 3, "pos_bytes_equal_array_last_point": 2, "pos_ptr_is_one_of_our_calc_calls": 2, "stop_kinds": {"OverX": 1, "OverY": 1, "NoConverge": 1}, "budget_exits_with_count_eq_budget": 0, "stop_count_plus1_eq_n": 3, "stop_conflicts": 0}, "notes": ["L17 (Level 17, DiffEq, 10+ scattered obstacles, 2 targets): sin(x)-y/2 = OverX n=5098 but execute_results reads n=1528 of the SAME buffer (obstacle truncation in place; pos = pts[1527]); y = OverY n=344 (no truncation); sqrt(0-y) = NoConverge n=1407 (no truncation)."]}
